      "updatedAt": "yesterday at 10:12 AM",
      "version": "V6",
      "markdown": "# Buyer Engage\n\nMonitors buyer activity across connected sources and drafts personalized outreach when meaningful engagement signals appear.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nBuyer Engage watches for specific engagement signals—website visits to high-intent pages, email opens on stalled threads, LinkedIn activity from a champion, or Salesforce activity from a decision maker—and drafts an outreach message the seller can accept, edit, or discard.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Watch the seller's active opportunities and target-account contacts.\n2. Trigger on strong engagement signals only—ignore low-value noise (unsubscribes, out-of-office, generic newsletter opens).\n3. When a signal fires, gather the relevant context: opportunity stage, last touch, buyer role, and the signal itself.\n4. Draft a short, personalized message referencing the signal and a clear next step.\n5. Match the seller's usual tone; keep the draft under 90 words.\n6. Present the draft for review before any send.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never send outreach without seller approval.\n- Do not reference private buyer information the seller wouldn't already know from Salesforce.\n- Skip signals that arrive outside the buyer's likely working hours.\n- Respect any \"do not contact\" flag on the Salesforce contact record.\n\n## Example output\n\nWhen a champion revisits the pricing page on a stalled opportunity, the seller sees a proposed follow-up referencing the revisit and offering a concise, single next step—no boilerplate.\n",
      "linked": true
