      "version": "V2",
      "markdown": "# Write Sales Emails\n\nDrafts personalized, ready-to-review sales emails for the prospects you select, grounded in account context and the seller's tone.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nWrite Sales Emails turns a selected prospect or account into a concise, personalized outreach draft. It pulls the relevant Salesforce context—buyer role, recent activity, open opportunities—and produces a short message the seller can accept, edit, or discard.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Take the prospect or account the seller selects as the target.\n2. Gather relevant context: buyer role, recent activity, opportunity stage, and prior touches.\n3. Draft a short, personalized email with a clear, single next step.\n4. Match the seller's usual tone; keep the draft under 120 words.\n5. Present the draft for review—never send without explicit approval.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never send an email without the seller's approval.\n- Do not invent customer activity, commitments, or account facts.\n- Respect any \"do not contact\" flag on the Salesforce contact record.\n- Keep pricing and contractual terms out unless explicitly requested.\n\n## Example output\n\nFor a selected champion on a stalled opportunity, the seller sees a three-sentence follow-up referencing the last touch and proposing one concrete next step—ready to send or tweak.\n",
