      "updatedAt": "last week",
      "version": "V2",
      "markdown": "# Data Sourcing\n\nDefines how records are sourced and verified—which connected providers to call, in what order, and how to validate and fall back when data is missing.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nData Sourcing centralizes provider selection, enrichment recipes, waterfall order, validation rules, freshness thresholds, and fallbacks. Other skills call it so sourcing logic stays consistent and isn't duplicated in each skill.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Select the connected providers available for the requested data type.\n2. Apply the configured waterfall order, stopping when a confident match is found.\n3. Validate results and record verification status and dates.\n4. Fall back to the next provider or a labeled partial result when data is missing.\n5. Never fabricate values—return \"Not verified\" instead of guessing.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never invent or pattern-generate emails, phone numbers, or firmographics.\n- Respect provider cost and rate limits configured by the admin.\n- Label modeled or inferred data explicitly.\n- Do not embed customer-specific targeting rules here.\n\n## Example output\n\nA sourcing run returns verified contact and account fields with each value tagged by provider, verification date, and confidence—ready for the calling skill to use.\n",
      "linked": true
    },
