      "updatedAt": "last week",
      "version": "V4",
      "markdown": "# Executive Brief\n\nSummarizes the week's pipeline movement, wins, and risks into a concise brief the seller can share with leadership.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nExecutive Brief reviews the seller's pipeline over the trailing week and produces a leadership-ready summary: what moved, what closed, what slipped, and where the seller needs help. It favors signal over detail so a manager can read it in under a minute.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Analyze the seller's opportunities for the trailing seven days.\n2. Summarize material stage, amount, and close-date changes.\n3. Call out closed-won and closed-lost outcomes with a one-line reason.\n4. Surface the two or three deals most at risk and why.\n5. End with the specific asks where the seller needs manager support.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never invent pipeline values, outcomes, or activity.\n- Separate confirmed facts from inferred risks.\n- Respect Salesforce permissions and sharing rules.\n- Keep the brief scannable—lead with the takeaway, not the data dump.\n\n## Example output\n\nA Friday brief opens with the week's headline—two deals advanced, one slipped—then lists the at-risk opportunities and a short ask for each, ready to paste into a leadership channel.\n",
