      "updatedBy": "Zubin Keith",
      "updatedAt": "yesterday at 8:00 AM",
      "version": "V6",
      "markdown": "# Quota Health Check\n\nDistills everything happening across the seller's book into the three things that matter most this week—with the reason each made the cut.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nQuota Health Check scans the seller's pipeline, activity, and signals and ranks them down to a short list of three: the highest-impact opportunity, the biggest emerging risk, and the single best net-new play. Each item names the signal that raised it and a concrete next step.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Review the seller's open opportunities, recent activity, and buying signals.\n2. Score candidates by expected impact and urgency.\n3. Select the top three, favoring variety—one to advance, one to protect, one to open.\n4. For each, state the signal that raised it and one concrete next step.\n5. Keep the whole thing to three items—resist expanding the list.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never invent activity, signals, or pipeline values.\n- Separate confirmed facts from inferred priorities.\n- Respect Salesforce permissions and sharing rules.\n- Hold the list to exactly three—the value is in the ruthless prioritization.\n\n## Example output\n\nMonday's list reads: advance the Globex renewal (champion re-engaged), protect the Initech deal (close date slipped twice), and open Northwind (new funding), each with a one-line next step.\n",
      "linked": true
    }
